  "notes": "Confessional alt-pop on a programmed/played hybrid bed: 73–105 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and uptempos reaching 118–130, so the session spans 73–130. The harmony is modal rather than functional — \"riff-based two- and three-chord vamps (I–IV–V or i–VII–IV) with a droning tonic\" and \"open-string guitar tunings keep a pedal note under changes\" — which is `maxChords` 3, a vamp-weighted harmonic rhythm and mixolydian in the scales. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick on 1 and the '&' of 2\", \"snare 2&4 played hard with a dry room\" (a high accent tier with a tight ghost), and the closing constraint — \"the fill vocabulary is minimal — a crash, not a roll\" — which puts the hat rolls at 0.03, the fills at every 16 bars and a crash in the percs. The melody is the entry's strongest claim and is encoded as written: it is \"a *rhythmic* instrument — long syllable-dense phrases that push against the barline, small pitch range, spoken-to-sung contour\", so the density runs 6–12 in a 20-semitone band with long phrases. The stated irregular 10- and 12-bar verses are authored in `sectionBars`. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 92.",
